## Exercise 7.3




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
t.url <- "http://stat.ethz.ch/Teaching/Datasets/WBL/varve.dat"
d.varve <- ts(scan(t.url)[201:550])
```
:::




### A




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot(d.varve)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](rtp02_exercise_07_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-8-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::




Yes, there is a need for log-transform.

### B




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot(log(d.varve))
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](rtp02_exercise_07_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-9-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::




The time series it not stationary by simply using log-tranformation. We try differencing.




::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
plot(diff(d.varve, 10))
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](rtp02_exercise_07_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-10-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::




Looks good now.
